# Sympath - plucked and bowed strings over a buzzing bridge.
#
# Each note is a string lying over a wide, curved bridge. Once it swings far
# enough it strikes the bridge, and every strike rings it: a bright buzz on
# every cycle that lasts as long as the string swings wide enough to reach.
# `bridge` is how much, `curve` how wide a swing it takes.
#
# Under the played strings lie sympathetic strings tuned to `sa` (the tonic)
# and `scale`, which ring on the notes of the scale. `chikari` strikes the
# drone strings with each note. A tanpura plucks its four strings by itself
# through a `cycle` of beats while a note is held, its first string set by
# `first`. With one voice, `meend` slides from note to note; `gamak` (and
# the mod wheel) shakes the note, and pressure pulls the string up.
#
# 96 patches in eight families: sitar, sarod, veena, drone, east, bowed,
# fiddle and bridge. All ten scales are used somewhere.
#
# Every patch but Init carries eight named macros. Destinations are
# numbered as in Sympath.h's MacroDest: #1 bridge, #2 curve, #3 pluck,
# #4 position, #5 sustain, #6 bright, #7 tarbs, #8 chikari, #9 meend,
# #10 gamak, #11 velocity, #12 volume, #13 pitch (24 semitones a unit).
# A plucked string gets Buzz, Bright, Longer, Tarbs (or Mid String),
# Chikari (or Hard), Gamak, Slide (one voice) or Touch, and Low; a tanpura
# Jawari, Round and Waver; a bowed string Grip (the bow's pressure). A
# macro whose knob has no room left goes the other way under the opposite
# name (Clean, Dark, Shorter, Dry, ...); patches low in the range go High.
# Where a macro at full moves the level by more than 1.2 dB, a volume
# route takes it back out.

machine Sympath
role tune

patch Init family=sitar note=61 range=48..84

patch Sitar family=sitar note=61 range=48..84 role=lead
  # One string, sliding between notes, the sympathetic strings ringing under it.
  set macro1 "Buzz"
  set macro2 "Bright"
  set macro3 "Longer"
  set macro4 "Tarbs"
